3.5 Important Classes

Target (models/target.py) — @dataclass
- Fields: target: str, created_at: str (ISO-8601 UTC default), status: str (default DEFAULT_TARGET_STATUS)
- Methods: to_dict(), from_dict(data)

Scope (models/scope.py) — @dataclass
- Fields: in_scope: List[str], out_of_scope: List[str]
- Methods: to_dict(), from_dict(data)

TargetManager (core/target_manager.py)
- __init__(scope_manager: Optional[ScopeManager] = None)
- set_target(target_url, status=None) -> Target — atomic: validates structure → checks credentials → validates status → enforces scope → only then mutates self._current_target
- get_target() -> Optional[Target]
- get_target_url() -> Optional[str]
- update_status(status) -> Target
- clear()
- _sanitize_url_for_log(url) — strips credentials for safe logging

ScopeManager (core/scope_manager.py)
- __init__()
- load_scope(scope_dict) — validates then normalizes rules
- enforce_scope(resource) — raises OutOfScopeError if out; fails closed if no scope loaded
- is_in_scope(resource) -> bool — precedence: out-of-scope checked BEFORE in-scope
- _normalize_resource(resource) -> Optional[str] — handles hostname, URL, hostname:port; rejects whitespace; validates port range 1–65535
- _matches_rule(resource_host, rule) — exact match + strict *.domain wildcard (must not match root, must not match evil-example.com, must not match example.com.evil.com)

SensitiveDataFilter (core/logger.py) — logging.Filter
- SENSITIVE_PATTERNS (4 regexes): key=value, Bearer/Basic, Cookie/Authorization, credential URLs
- SECRET_FORMAT_PATTERNS (5 regexes): detects %s format strings that will receive secrets
- filter(record) — redacts args BEFORE message formatting; handles tuple/list and dict args
- _has_secret_format(msg), _is_secret_key(key), _redact_pattern(msg, patterns)

Settings (config/settings.py)
- get(key, default), set(key, value), update(dict)
- output_dir property (Path)
- Global singleton settings

3.6 Important Functions

- validate_target(target) (utils/validation.py) — rejects empty, whitespace, missing scheme, unsupported scheme, missing netloc, credentials, invalid hostname, invalid port
- validate_scope_entry(entry) — validates domain, wildcard, or URL scope entries
- validate_scope(scope_dict) — requires in_scope key, non-empty list, validates all entries
- ensure_directory(path), verify_output_path(file_path, base_dir), write_json_file(path, data), read_json_file(path) (utils/file_utils.py)
- setup_logger(name, level) (core/logger.py) — idempotent, respects explicit level or settings

