PART 4 — PHASE-BY-PHASE HISTORY

PHASE 01 — Foundation & Target Management

Name

Phase 01: Foundation & Target Management

Purpose

Establish the foundational layer of the XENON web security assessment platform: project configuration, target management, scope management, target validation, scope enforcement, common data models, logging, exception handling, file/output utilities, CLI entry point, and foundation-level testing. Does NOT perform vulnerability scanning or detection.

Why It Was Created

XENON was rebuilt from a broad AI-assistant vision into a web security assessment platform. Phase 01 was created as the mandatory security foundation — before any scanning could happen, XENON needed to know what target is authorized and what is in/out of scope. As README §6.5 states: "No future XENON module should be allowed to perform an assessment request against a resource that the Scope Manager determines to be out of scope."

