10.8 Security Rules

- Scope safety: Out-of-scope resources must never be treated as valid assessment targets.
- Explicit scope precedence: Out-of-scope rules override broad wildcard rules.
- Input validation: Target and scope input validated before use.
- Sensitive data: Do not log passwords, API keys, access tokens, session cookies, authorization headers, secrets.
- Path safety: File utilities must avoid unsafe/unintended filesystem paths.
- Deterministic decisions: Scope decisions must be deterministic and reproducible.
- Fail-closed: No scope loaded → out of scope; malformed resource → out of scope.
- Atomic state: Target state only mutated after all validations pass.
- Credential rejection: URLs with embedded username/password rejected.

